@tradition tiles-ladder
// Tiles ladder (0.60.7, the user's pick): a friendly weekly Tiles round-robin on Saturday afternoons in the bow lounge,
// with a chalkboard for the week's winner. Olu Farouk keeps the ladder. The boards are Tiles night's (decor tilesNight);
// the results would be the Tiles engineer's (section 23).
k: 450
title: Tiles ladder
when: weekly saturday
at: 15:00-16:30
min: 25
jitter: 15
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
hold: 1
who: farouk-olu always, rina 90%, lounge-regular 40%, everyone 10%
anim: play
host: farouk-olu
from: farouk-olu
ties: decor tilesNight
invite: host=farouk-olu odds=30% line="Tiles ladder this afternoon. You're on the board. Bottom rung, but on the board."


== mail
- Tiles ladder tomorrow at {time} in the bow lounge. Everyone plays everyone. The winner's name goes on the chalkboard.

== ask
- Tiles ladder this afternoon. Everyone plays everyone.
- Fancy the ladder? Your name could be on the chalkboard.

== here
- Who's next? Me? Already?
- Good game. Rematch on the ladder next week.
- The chalkboard's watching. No pressure.   #funny

== thanks
- You play your way round the Tiles ladder in the bow lounge, one friendly game after another, under the chalkboard.

== chatter
- Tiles ladder today. My name was up there once.   #funny
- Who's top of the chalkboard this week?
- The ladder's friendly. Mostly. Nearly.   #funny
